{"event": "report", "t": 1795258019.303, "claim": "fixed", "text": " (profile `retail_dw_master`, DuckDB at `/app/database/retail.duckdb`, schema `analytics`), `models/sources.yml`, and `models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql`.\n- The model reads `FACT_MARKETING_SPEND` from the warehouse. Spend is at the campaign-day level, with one row per campaign per channel.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- **Spend source:** the marketing spend table is `ANALYTICS.FACT_MARKETING_SPEND`, which the existing `stg_fact_marketing_spend` model also reads.\n- **`/app/dbt_transforms` doesn't exist.** I used the reference project at `/app/dbt_models_duckdb` instead.\n- **Channel key:** each campaign gets the single channel with the highest total spend, with ties broken by lowest key. All spend and revenue are then combined per campaign.\n- **Same-day rows:** six campaign-days have two channel rows. These are summed into one row per campaign per day.\n- **Payback definitions:** `payback_ratio = cumulative_revenue / cumulative_spend` and `is_paid_back = cumulative_revenue >= cumulative_spend`. Both are my reading of \"how much of the investment has been recouped.\" Cumulative totals are computed from unrounded sums and rounded at the end.\n- **Snowflake:** I did not add a Snowflake profile or target, because `DB_TYPE=duckdb`.\n\n**Verification**\n- The table has 994 rows across 30 campaigns, with one row per campaign and `days_since_cohort`.\n- Column names and types match the spec.\n- No negative values, and cumulative spend and revenue never decrease within a campaign.\n- For every campaign, the last-row cumulative totals match the source totals within 0.01.\n- Every campaign has exactly one `channel_key`, and it is the top-spend channel.\n\n**One thing to know**\n- My first build created the table with uppercase column names, and that made dbt fail on a name clash. I dropped that table, which was my own artifact, and rebuilt it. The current table lives in the `ANALYTICS` schema because DuckDB treats `analytics` and `ANALYTICS` as the same schema.\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
